+# Story 2.1: Playtest Protocol + Capture Tooling (run-founders-kid)
+
+Status: review
+
+<!-- Note: Validation is optional. Run validate-create-story for quality check before dev-story. -->
+
+## Story
+
+As the founder of FinLit Street (Moses),
+I want a complete, runnable playtest protocol — a script, a fillable per-session scorecard, and machine session-capture tooling in the game,
+so that the E2 playtest gate can be run unaided with the founder's kid (design anchor, 9) and the evidence (timed rows, exact quotes, gate verdict, open-question reads) lands in a filed scorecard per session.
+
+**Scope note (dispatch briefing, authoritative over the sprint-plan wording):** the sprint plan lists e2-1 as the human-run session ("M, Moses-owned"). The run itself is inherently human; this story ships the protocol + tooling the run depends on — the script exists (`docs/playtest-script.md`, mined not duplicated), the **scorecard** is new, and the **playtest-mode capture** (`--playtest` session logger + observer overlay) is new. The founder's-kid run then happens outside this dispatch, filing the filled scorecard per the plan's AC. `pr_review: true` on this job.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+1. Story file exists at `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/stories/e2-1-playtest-protocol-run-founders-kid.md` in the gds-create-story format, status `ready-for-dev` (this file).
+2. `docs/playtest-script.md` — the 15-min gate script — is mined (not duplicated) and updated with: playtest-mode launch command, session-log location, and a pointer to the scorecard.
+3. `docs/playtest-scorecard.md` — NEW fillable per-session scorecard: session header (kid band, device, build/commit, observer), timed rows (first-wage <60s PASS/FAIL with seconds; FIND WORK unaided), observation rows covering **every** AC row of the script with exact-quote fields, gate scoring table, open-question evidence (reroll policy / no-parents tone / LLM-vs-scripted), surprising-things log, and the filing convention (`_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/playtest-scorecards/<date>-<kid>.md`).
+4. Playtest-mode flag `--playtest` on the game: a `PlaytestSession` logger (RefCounted, **not** an autoload — the two-autoload cap is E3) records a JSONL timeline to `user://playtest/session-<ts>.jsonl` (overridable via `--playtest-log <path>`), with events: `session_begin`, `boot`, `age_picked`, `street_name` (+ `street_name_reroll`), `lottery`, `reroll_attempt`, `job_picked`, `first_wage`, `buy`, `upgrade`, `repair`, `event`, `tutor_open`, `league_open`, `new_game` — each line JSON-friendly with `elapsed_ms` and unix `ts`.
+5. Observer overlay: a `PlaytestChip` HUD label (session timer + event count) visible only in playtest mode **and** debug builds (arch §Debug Tools feature-tag rule); zero gameplay behavior change when the flag is absent.
+6. Capture setup documented: the existing `tools/capture.gd` rig command for evidence stills (windowed off-screen, never headless) referenced from the protocol docs.
+7. COPPA floor: the log contains no free text and no real names — street names are generator-first, age data is bracket bands only (project-context COPPA rule).
+8. Tests: NEW headless bare runner `game/tests/test_playtest_session.gd` (the pre-GUT suite pattern; e3-3 migrates) covering flag/path parsing, JSONL shape + ordering + elapsed monotonicity, single-record semantics for `first_wage` (guarded by `seen_first_wage`), reroll-attempt capture, disabled-session no-op, and a scene-level boot flow (seeded save → `_on_job_picked` → first wage auto-recorded). Both bare runners green; the two-invocation headless import gate clean; capture rig smoke-tested windowed off-screen.
+9. Commit on `finlit-e2-1`, push, `gh pr create --base main` titled "feat: e2-1 playtest protocol + capture tooling" with a **Decisions & rationale** section. Never merge.
