+## Dev Notes
+
+### Architecture & design constraints (non-negotiable)
+
+- **E2 runs on the current flat slice** (arch §Project Structure, A2: spike layout is evidence, not the template; migration is incremental from E3). New code lands flat: `game/scripts/playtest_session.gd`, `game/tests/test_playtest_session.gd`. E3 re-homes it (candidate home: `tools/` or `scripts/ui/` — note for e3-1/e3-3).
+- **No autoloads** — the two-autoload cap (`GameState`, `SaveManager`) lands in E3. `PlaytestSession` is a `RefCounted` instantiated by `street.gd` when the flag is present. Do NOT add an `[autoload]` entry.
+- **Engines stay pure** — the logger is observer tooling in the UI layer only; it never mutates state and no engine code references it.
+- **Debug overlays are excluded from release exports via feature tags** (arch §Debug Tools): overlay chip gated on `OS.has_feature("debug")` AND the flag. The logger itself is flag-gated only (a release playtest build is not a thing in E2, and the log is harmless/off by default).
+- **JSON-friendly data only** (project-context): plain Dictionary/String/int/float/bool/null; the log's `elapsed_ms`/`ts` write as ints; test assertions must re-cast with `int()` after `JSON.parse_string` (Godot parses JSON ints as floats).
+- **COPPA floor** (project-context): no free text, no real names. Street names are generator-first (dice-rolled), age = bracket band. Nothing typed by the kid exists in the game to log. Call this out in the PR.
+- **Deferred frame semantics** (project-context): the chip only changes text/visibility — no sizing/measurement the same frame it's added. The tscn edit declares the node; `_ready` toggles visibility.
+- **`pressed` never fires on disabled buttons** — the REROLL stub is disabled (`reroll.disabled = not FinLitLifeLottery.is_reroll_allowed()`); capture attempts via `gui_input` on the button, gated to playtest mode (behavior unchanged otherwise).
