+### Testing standards summary
+
+- Bare-runner pattern until GUT lands (arch A9 / project-context Testing Rules): `godot --headless --path game --script res://tests/test_economy.gd` is the suite; the new runner follows the same shape. GUT migration (e3-3) moves both; the `test_*` naming keeps them findable.
+- Scene tests add nodes into the tree and drive from `_process`; backends get path overrides (`LocalJsonBackend.new("user://test_...")`) so real `user://` saves are never touched (project-context Testing Rules). The playtest log path is injected the same way for scene tests (`--playtest-log user://test_playtest_sessions/session.jsonl` on the runner invocation).
+- The suite runs BOTH ways: plain (asserts playtest OFF: no overlay, no log, `_playtest == null`) and `-- --playtest --playtest-log <test path>` (asserts ON). `first_wage` timing: `_on_job_picked` presets `_wage_timer = WAGE_DROP_SECONDS`, so the first wage lands next frame — the test asserts `job_picked` then `first_wage` in order with `elapsed_ms` sane (<5s), and that a second `_pay_wage()` call records no duplicate.
+
+### Project Structure Notes
+
+- Current flat `game/` tree is the E2 playtest build and stays runnable (arch A2). `tools/capture.gd` is the established tool home — the new logger is a runtime script (lives in `scripts/`), not a tool. Target-layout home for E3+: `scripts/ui/` (observer surface) with the JSONL writer either there or in `tools/` — decide in e3-1's re-home pass.
+
+### Project Context Rules
+
+- Godot 4.7.1, GDScript only, static typing everywhere; `snake_case` funcs/vars, `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` consts, `_prefixed` privates, `class_name` PascalCase.
+- Pure-logic engines own ALL state mutation; UI scenes only render state and forward input. The logger only reads (never writes state).
+- Autoload cap: exactly two — do not add one.
+- All game data JSON-friendly; null for absent optionals, never `""`/`-1` sentinels.
+- COPPA floor: no chat/free-text/real names; LLM payloads pseudonymous. Session logs follow the same rule.
+- Debug overlays excluded from release exports via feature tags.
+- `godot --headless --path game --import` then `godot --headless --path game --quit-after 600` is the parse gate; captures run WINDOWED off-screen (`--position -3000,-3000`), never headless.
+- Float frame-delta accumulators; clamp `delta = minf(delta, 0.25)` (not applicable to the logger — it uses `Time.get_ticks_msec()`, not frame deltas).
+- GDScript fails silently: every error path recovers or surfaces (log-open failure → `push_warning`, game continues without logging).
