+# Playtest scorecard — FinLit Street (fill per session)
+
+**The E2 gate's evidence file.** Run the session with `docs/playtest-script.md`
+open; fill this card as you go (or right after, from the session log — the
+machine timeline makes the timed rows exact). When full, **file it**:
+`_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/playtest-scorecards/<yyyy-mm-dd>-<kid>.md`
+(next to the spec, per story e2-1 AC). Every session files one card, even
+failed runs — a broken read is data.
+
+## Session header
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Date + start/end time | |
+| Kid (band / age) | |
+| Device (phone/desktop, size) | |
+| Build (branch / commit / `godot --version`) | |
+| Observer | |
+| Session log path | `user://playtest/session-<ts>.jsonl` |
+| Screen recording? (optional) | |
+
+## Before you start (2 min)
+
+1. Delete any prior save (`user://finlit_save.json`) for a true first launch.
+2. Launch in playtest mode — the machine timeline records every event below:
+   ```bash
+   godot --path game -- --playtest
+   ```
+   (Log: `user://playtest/session-<ts>.jsonl`. Optional evidence stills —
+   deterministic before/after frames, run BEFORE the kid arrives and AFTER
+   the session, windowed off-screen — never headless, never while the kid
+   plays:)
+   ```bash
+   env -u DEEPSEEK_API_KEY godot --path game --position -3000,-3000 \
+     --script res://tools/capture.gd -- --out /tmp/finlit-capture
+   ```
+3. Note the clock. Observer rules: **no helping, no explaining** — "what do
+   you think you do?" is the only answer.
+
+## Timed rows (machine-measured)
+
+Read these off the session log (JSONL, one event per line, `elapsed_ms` from
+session start; all timestamps UTC; JSON ints come back as floats — re-cast
+with `int()`). Each `boot` event starts a game segment: read timed rows from
+the FIRST segment unless the kid hit 🔄 NEW GAME, in which case use that
+segment's `boot` (rows key off the latest `boot`).
+
+| Row | From the log | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| First wage <60s | first `first_wage` after the latest `boot`: `elapsed_ms` ÷ 1000 = ____ s | PASS / FAIL |
+| FIND WORK found unaided | `job_picked` present before any observer word; time from its segment's `boot` = ____ s | PASS / FAIL |
+
+## Observation rows (per script AC — every row, no summaries)
+
+### Minute 0–2 — first launch & the life lottery
+- Age pick: instant / hesitant · bracket: ____
+- Street name: 🎲 NEW NAME mashed ____ times (`street_name_reroll` count) or accepted immediately
+- **Life lottery read (the key read):** cartoonish-with-a-path or unfair/sad?
+  Exact words: ______________________
+- Reroll attempts: `reroll_attempt` count = ____ · frustrated? ______________________
+
+### Minute 2–5 — first job & first wage
+- Job chosen: ____ · why (ask after): affection vs pay? ______________________
+- First-wage reaction (coin blip + balance bump): noticed? smile/comment? ______________________
+- Any label longer than 3 words read aloud or stumbled on? ______________________
+
+### Minute 5–12 — the core loop
+- ≥2 assets bought? Which? Names land ("Sunny Duplex")? ______________________
+- Upgraded once? Noticed the building grow / level stars? ______________________
+- Event survived (`event` events in log): 🔧 Burst Pipe — **can the kid say what
+  it cost THEIR building?** Ask "what just happened to your duplex?" Exact
+  words: ______________________ · 📈 Rate Hike with no debt — did "no effect"
+  make sense? ______________________
+- ❓ Mrs. K opened? scripted or LLM (`tutor_open` mode)? comment? ______________________
+- 🏆 league opened? Reaction to the YOU row (wealth *climbed*)? ______________________
+- Confusion / boredom / "what do I do now?" moments (with times): ______________________
+
+### Minute 12–15 — wrap questions
+1. "Want to play again tomorrow?" **D1 read:** YES / NO · if no, what would make it a yes? ______________________
+2. "Show me your street." Ownership narration ("this is MY snack cart, it pays me")? ______________________
+3. "Was anything unfair?" (lottery read #2) ______________________
+4. "What would you buy next?" ______________________
+
+## Scoring the gate
+
+| Acceptance criterion | Evidence | PASS / FAIL |
+|---|---|---|
+| Minute one: lottery + job + wage ≤60s, ≤3-word labels | timed row above | |
+| Disaster teach: kid states what it cost *their* building | quote above | |
+| Unaided: ≥2 assets, 1 upgrade, 1 event survived, asks to play tomorrow | ticks + Q1 | |
+
+## Open-question evidence for canon (log + quotes)
+
+- **Reroll policy (OPEN):** `reroll_attempt` count + reactions (a transparent
+  tap probe on the disabled stub records left-click/touch attempts only): ______________________
+- **No-parents tone (sensitivity, N21):** warm vs sad read: ______________________
+- **LLM tutor vs scripted (integrate-vs-drop):** which preferred, if compared: ______________________
+
+## Surprising things
+
+Anything at all that wasn't asked — write it down; it goes into the next
+spec revision. ______________________
+
+---
+
+## Session log reference (what the machine records)
+
+Every line: `{"event": ..., "elapsed_ms": <ms since start>, "ts": <unix>, ...}`
+(`elapsed_ms`/`ts` parse as floats — re-cast with `int()`). Event order is
+record order; the timeline is the truth for timed rows.
+
+| Event | When | Payload |
+|---|---|---|
+| `session_begin` | log opened | version, log_path |
+| `boot` | game loaded | street_name, bracket |
+| `age_picked` | age screen answered | bracket |
+| `street_name` / `street_name_reroll` | name accepted / 🎲 mashed | name / — |
+| `lottery` | life accepted | housing, traits |
+| `reroll_attempt` | tap on the disabled REROLL | — |
+| `job_picked` | job chosen | job |
+| `first_wage` | first wage lands (once) | amount |
+| `buy` / `upgrade` / `repair` | street mutations | type+name / name+level / name |
+| `event` | market-tick event card | title, effect, cost |
+| `tutor_open` | ❓ Mrs. K | mode (scripted / llm / compare) |
+| `league_open` | 🏆 panel | — |
+| `new_game` | 🔄 NEW GAME reset | — |
+
+COPPA-safe by construction: no free text, no real names (street names are
+dice-rolled), age = bracket band only. Logs live under `user://playtest/`
+(not in the repo, never committed).
